  "goodToKnow": "Fesseln means to tie up or shackle: jemanden an Händen und Füßen fesseln. Figuratively, it means to captivate or grip: Das Buch hat mich gefesselt, and fesselnd means gripping. Ans Bett gefesselt sein means to be bedridden. Die Fessel is a shackle, and also the ankle area of a person or horse; die Fußfessel is an electronic ankle tag. Note the ich-form: ich fessle. From an old Germanic root meaning to fasten."
